            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0331" n="229" xml:id="pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.428/534</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lindsay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic">August 29,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 636</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I duly brought to the notice of the
                    Canadian Government the contents of your Note No. 357 of the 25th instant,
                    informing me of a clerical error in the text of the Sockeye Salmon
                    Convention.</p>
                <p>I have now the honour to inform you that I have received a telegram from the
                    Governor General of Canada stating that the Government of Canada concurs in the
                    corrections.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. C. Lindsay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
